---
import { statSync } from 'node:fs';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Prompt from '../components/Prompt.astro';
import AsciiTorus from '../components/AsciiTorus.astro';

const notes = [
    { file: 'Fermat_s_Last_Theorem.pdf', title: 'Self-Learning Fermat & Modularity' },
    { file: 'Fermat_s_Last_Theorem_2.pdf', title: 'Self-Learning Deformation Theory (R = T)' },
    { file: 'Optimization_and_Approximation_in_Route_Planning.pdf', title: 'Optimization and Approximation in Route Planning' },
].map(n => {
    const bytes = statSync(`public/pdf/${n.file}`).size;   // builds run from the project root
    return { ...n, size: bytes >= 1e6 ? `${(bytes / 1e6).toFixed(1)}M` : `${Math.round(bytes / 1e3)}K` };
});
---

<Base description="Math at UBC and on my own: an interactive ASCII torus, elliptic curves, and notes on Fermat's Last Theorem.">
    <header>
        <h1 class="page-title">Math</h1>
        <div class="subtitle">Half of a Combined Major — and the reason for the donut below</div>
    </header>

    <section class="section">
        <Prompt path="~/math" command="./torus --interactive" />
        <AsciiTorus />
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <Prompt path="~/math" command="cat elliptic_curve.txt" />
        <div class="content">
            <p>An elliptic curve over ℂ, <strong>E : y² = x³ + ax + b</strong>, is secretly a donut.</p>
            <p>Take a lattice <strong>Λ = ω₁ℤ + ω₂ℤ</strong> and glue opposite sides of its parallelogram:
               you get the torus <strong>ℂ/Λ</strong>, and the Weierstrass map
               <strong>z ↦ (℘(z), ℘′(z))</strong> identifies it with E(ℂ).</p>
            <p class="legend">
                <span class="ta">━━</span> sides parallel to ω₁ — glued first<br />
                <span class="tb">━━</span> sides parallel to ω₂ — glued second
            </p>
            <p class="muted">Wiles proved Fermat's Last Theorem by showing that curves like this (over ℚ) are modular.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <Prompt path="~/math" command="ls -lh notes/" />
        <div class="notes">
            {notes.map(n => (
                <a class="note" href={`/pdf/${n.file}`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                    <span class="note-perm">-rw-r--r--</span>
                    <span class="note-size">{n.size}</span>
                    <span class="note-title">{n.title}</span>
                </a>
            ))}
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <Prompt path="~/math" command="cd ../courses" />
        <p>The coursework side lives in <a href="/courses">~/courses</a>.</p>
    </section>
</Base>

<style>
    .page-title { font-family: var(--font-header); }

    .legend { margin-top: 10px !important; }
    .legend .ta { color: var(--prompt-path); }
    .legend .tb { color: var(--prompt-user); }

    .notes { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px; }
    .note {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: auto 4.5em 1fr;
        gap: 14px;
        padding: 6px 10px;
        border: 1px solid transparent;
        border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;
        border-radius: 6px;
        color: var(--text-color);
    }
    .note:hover { border-color: rgba(158, 206, 106, 0.4); background: var(--bg-color2); opacity: 1; }
    .note-perm, .note-size { color: var(--sub-header-color); }
    .note-size { text-align: right; }
    .note-title { color: var(--link-color); }

    @media (max-width: 600px) {
        .note { grid-template-columns: 4em 1fr; }
        .note-perm { display: none; }
    }
</style>
